  "commits_data": [
    {
      "id": "61e66c37abb1b7f59726e4407ac8dd53e6b75cac",
      "short_id": "61e66c37",
      "created_at": "2021-08-31T19:19:05.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "49240e23b4cf890df67d81d1900f313d1193db8c"
      ],
      "title": "cmake: lemon: allow overriding lemon CC setting",
      "message": "cmake: lemon: allow overriding lemon CC setting\n\nWhen cross-compiling wireshark the lemon tool should be built\nusing the host machine compiler to be run on the host. Before\ncmake this was done via autotools CC_FOR_BUILD but cmake only\nsupports one compiler toolchain per build and requires some\nworkarounds like running cmake twice using separately defined\ntoolchains.\n\nThis gets ugly and complicated fast when considering multiple\ntoolchains, especially for a simple tool like lemon, so just\nallow builds to override the C compiler and wipe the cflags.\n\nThis way systems like Gentoo/ChromeOS/Yocto with a properly\nsetup cross-compile environment can just point to the native\nBUILD_CC or similar while minimizing complexity.\n",
      "author_name": "Adrian Ratiu",
      "author_email": "adrian.ratiu@collabora.com",
      "authored_date": "2021-08-26T17:44:11.000+03:00",
      "committer_name": "Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2021-08-31T19:19:05.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/61e66c37abb1b7f59726e4407ac8dd53e6b75cac"
    },
    {
      "id": "49240e23b4cf890df67d81d1900f313d1193db8c",
      "short_id": "49240e23",
      "created_at": "2021-08-31T19:19:05.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "2dc8b74afccd2da2d64854f94be94b65b3595489"
      ],
      "title": "cmake: lemon: fix path to internal lemon tool",
      "message": "cmake: lemon: fix path to internal lemon tool\n\nWireshark fails to build when cross-compiling on Gentoo/ChromeOS\nsystems because the lemon command is not properly specified or\nincluded in PATH, failing with:\n\n/bin/sh: lemon: command not found\n\nThe relevant excerpt from build.ninja is:\n\nCOMMAND = cd ..._build/plugins/epan/mate && lemon -T.../tools/lemon/lempar.c\n-d. .../plugins/epan/mate/mate_grammar.lemon\n\nBy specifying the full path to \"lemon\" we ensure it is\nalways searched and found in the correct location.\n",
      "author_name": "Adrian Ratiu",
      "author_email": "adrian.ratiu@collabora.com",
      "authored_date": "2021-08-25T20:13:03.000+03:00",
      "committer_name": "Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2021-08-31T19:19:05.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/49240e23b4cf890df67d81d1900f313d1193db8c"
    }
  ],
